        `,buttons:["Start {downsell_name}"]}]}],o3="From an enterprise CRM partner's AI-agent session offer",o4=[{id:"free-assessment-offer--saas--1",industry:"saas",origin:"written",page:{url:"{website}/assessment",sections:[{kind:"hero",eyebrow:"The offer from {event_title}",headline:"From knowing the {mechanism_name} to running it on your own network",sub:"A free cost-per-stop assessment, then a one-depot pilot you pay for only when it hits the KPIs we agree before we start.",cta:"Book a free {call_name}"},{kind:"steps",heading:"What you get",items:[{title:"1 · Cost-per-stop assessment",body:"We review last month's routes, price every stop and failed attempt, and rank the leaks by what they cost you. Outcome: a clear view of where the saving is, and where it isn't."},{title:"2 · Design for your first depot",body:"The replan rules, consolidation logic and guardrails for one depot, built on your data. What the system proposes and what your planners approve is set out in writing."},{title:"3 · A pilot in your real operation",body:"One depot, {timeframe}, running alongside your existing planner and telematics."},{title:"4 · Planner enablement",body:"Walkthroughs for planners and dispatchers: when to trust the plan, when to override it, and how to improve it week by week."}]},{kind:"text",heading:"Pilot terms",body:"We carry the setup cost. You pay only when the pilot hits the cost-per-stop and on-time KPIs we agree on day one. {guarantee}."},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Who it's for",items:["{icp_size} {icp_industry} businesses running their own fleet or a mixed carrier network","{icp_roles}, transport managers and the finance lead who owns the delivery budget"]},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Why {company_name}",items:["{social_proof}","Built for planners, not for data teams","No lock-in to one carrier or one system"]},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Working principles",items:["Planners approve the plan; the system proposes it","Every saving is shown against your own baseline","One depot before the network"]},{kind:"cta",heading:"Book a free 30-minute {call_name}",label:"Book my assessment",note:"No purchase attached. The assessment takes about two hours of your team's time, spread over a week."}]}},{id:"free-assessment-offer--consulting--1",industry:"consulting",origin:"written",page:{url:"{website}/growth-review",sections:[{kind:"hero",eyebrow:"The offer from {event_title}",headline:"From understanding the {mechanism_name} to climbing it in your own business",sub:"A free Growth Review, then a first 30 days together with {guarantee}.",cta:"Book a free {call_name}"},{kind:"steps",heading:"What you get",items:[{title:"1 · The Growth Review",body:"We score your business on all five rungs, list the decisions that still wait for you, and find the ceiling that's holding growth. Outcome: the two changes that would free you first."},{title:"2 · Your handover plan",body:"Who owns which decision, the weekly rhythm that replaces you in the room, and the one hire (if any) that makes it hold."},{title:"3 · The first 30 days",body:"Coaching as you hand over the first three decisions, with your team in the room."},{title:"4 · Team enablement",body:"Short sessions for the people taking decisions over: what they own, when to escalate, and how to report back."}]},{kind:"text",heading:"Terms",body:"The Growth Review is free. If you continue into {offer_name}, {guarantee}."},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Who it's for",items:["Founders of {icp_size} {icp_industry}","Owners whose business has grown but whose calendar hasn't emptied"]},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Why {company_name}",items:["{social_proof}","Coaches who have built and stepped back from their own businesses","A method, not motivation"]},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Working principles",items:["Your team owns the decisions we hand over; we don't","We only promise what we'll measure","If the programme isn't right for you, we'll say so on the call"]},{kind:"cta",heading:"Book your free {call_name}",label:"Book my Growth Review",note:"30 minutes, no purchase attached."}]}},{id:"free-assessment-offer--services--1",industry:"services",origin:"written",page:{url:"{website}/assessment",sections:[{kind:"hero",eyebrow:"The offer from {event_title}",headline:"From seeing the {mechanism_name} to running it in your own firm",sub:"A free admin assessment, then {offer_name}, with {guarantee}.",cta:"Book a free {call_name}"},{kind:"steps",heading:"What you get",items:[{title:"1 · Admin leak assessment",body:"We trace a week of requests from intake to delivery and show you where partner hours go. Outcome: the handoffs worth fixing first, ranked by hours."},{title:"2 · Handoff design for one practice area",body:"Intake, triage and review routing for the area with the most volume, to your own templates."},{title:"3 · The pilot",body:"Our trained team takes on drafting and assembly in that practice area for {timeframe}, with turnaround tracked on every matter."},{title:"4 · Team enablement",body:"Walkthroughs for partners, associates and coordinators: what now arrives pre-sorted, what still needs them, and how to flag a problem."}]},{kind:"text",heading:"Pilot terms",body:"We carry the setup. There's {guarantee}."},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Who it's for",items:["{icp_size} {icp_industry}","{icp_roles}, practice leads and operations directors"]},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Why {company_name}",items:["{social_proof}","Every document reviewed by someone qualified to sign it off","Secure, compliant handling of client files"]},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Working principles",items:["Partners approve; our team prepares","Turnaround is measured, not promised","One practice area before the firm"]},{kind:"cta",heading:"Book a free {call_name}",label:"Book my assessment",note:"30 minutes. No purchase attached."}]}},{id:"free-assessment-offer--ai--1",industry:"ai",origin:"real",label:"Variation 1 · use-case discovery + readiness assessment (the full offer)",from:o3,page:{url:"{website}/assessment",sections:[{kind:"hero",eyebrow:"What we're offering today",headline:"Turning AI agent use cases into real service outcomes",sub:"This offer is designed to help support organisations move from understanding AI agent use cases to applying them inside the service platforms they already run, using the real scenarios from the session.",cta:"Book a {call_name}"},{kind:"text",body:"Rather than selling generic AI, this engagement focuses on specific, high-friction service problems, and shows how agents can reduce the load on your people, improve decisions and lower the cost of every case."},{kind:"steps",heading:"What you get",items:[{title:"1 · Use-case discovery and readiness assessment",body:"A structured working session on your service environment, grounded in the patterns from the session: a review of your current support setup; the hotspots where the load on agents is highest (fragmented context, repeated escalations); your processes mapped to the three core use cases (business enquiries with order and account context, a co-pilot for field engineers, and case resolution across several teams); and priorities set by operational impact, not experimentation for its own sake. Outcome: a clear view of where agents can realistically help today, and where they shouldn't be used yet."},{title:"2 · Agent design for the chosen use case(s)",body:"AI-driven workflows designed and configured inside your platform. Depending on the use case: understanding unstructured emails and cases; context assembled from the service platform, the ERP and related systems (no black-box summaries); drafted responses a person approves; live context for engineers in the field; and a continuous case picture for managers handling escalations. Principles applied: handle ambiguity without guessing or blocking the flow; partial resolution beats none; AI supports judgement and doesn't replace people; context over raw automation."},{title:"3 · Implementation in your real workflows",body:"Anchored in how work actually happens, not in idealised process maps: platform configuration; the data sources your teams already use (order history, asset records, case notes, knowledge base); a clear line between what the agent assembles and recommends and what people approve, act on or override; auditability and explainability built in. Outcome: agents that behave like assistants and co-pilots, not opaque automation."},{title:"4 · Adoption for agents, engineers and leaders",body:"Enablement that lowers resistance instead of adding complexity: role-based walkthroughs for frontline agents, field engineers and service managers; the agent positioned as a co-worker that takes mental load off; clear guidance on when to trust it, when to step in, and how to improve outcomes over time."}]},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Who this is for",items:["Organisations hitting service-complexity limits as volume grows","Scaling organisations seeing rising service costs and uneven outcomes","Enterprises focused on cost control, satisfaction scores and fewer escalations","Roles: service and CX leaders, operations heads, field service leaders, and executives responsible for service cost, quality and risk"]},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Why {company_name}",items:["Deep expertise in customer service and field service platforms","A real understanding of case complexity and agent load, not just automation","A platform-native approach, not generic AI tooling bolted on top","Experience designing AI that copes with ambiguity, keeps human judgement in place and improves decisions, not just speed","{social_proof}"]},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Working principles",items:["People in the loop by design","No guessing in customer-facing answers","Decisions stay explainable and auditable","AI supports agents, engineers and leaders; it doesn't replace them","Early intervention and clarity, not reactive firefighting"]},{kind:"cta",heading:"This isn't about experimenting with AI. It's about putting it to work responsibly.",label:"Book a {call_name}",note:"A free 30-minute walkthrough of the relevant use cases · a discussion focused on your service complexity · a no-obligation assessment grounded in your platform."}]}},{id:"free-assessment-offer--ai--2",industry:"ai",origin:"real",label:"Variation 2 · the shorter readiness-assessment version (six steps + credentials)",from:o3,page:{url:"{website}/readiness",sections:[{kind:"hero",eyebrow:"What we're offering today",headline:"Ready to take the next step with AI agents?",sub:"The {mechanism_name} assessment is designed to close the gap between connected data and real-time action. By resolving the routine queries automatically, it cuts your backlog and brings service costs down.",cta:"Lock in my assessment"},{kind:"text",body:"Give your support agents and field engineers room to be human, while autonomous agents handle the rest, so every customer gets an immediate, accurate and personal response."},{kind:"bullets",heading:"What you get: six essential steps",items:["Evaluate your data foundations and complexity hotspots (heavy agent load, fragmented context, repeated escalations)","Explore the three core use cases from the session","Make sure data security and access controls are in place","Choose the right language models","Set up log monitoring","Plan change management and the operational impact"]},{kind:"text",heading:"No cost, no obligation, no sale",body:"A half-day to one-day engagement, free. Outcome: a tailored roadmap with clear next steps to put agents live, a quick time to value and a clear return."},{kind:"bullets",heading:"Why {company_name}",items:["{social_proof}","Specialists in the four foundations of AI agents: customer data, platform, AI and personalisation"]},{kind:"text",heading:"What can you realistically expect?",body:"Better service on every channel, from the contact centre to the field. On each new job, your agents run a cycle of observing, evaluating, recommending and acting, step by step, learning and adapting until they reach the right outcome."},{kind:"cta",label:"Lock in my assessment",note:"Offered to people on the live session. Free."}]}}],o5=[{id:"trade-show-sequence--saas--1",industry:"saas",origin:"written",label:"Post-event follow-ups only · met + missed",steps:[{offset:"T+1 · met at the stand",role:"follow-up",channel:"email",sender:"{host_name}, {company_name}",subject:"{first_name}, following up on our chat at {trade_show}",body:oA`
